    text: 'If your birthday falls on the first day of any month — for example January 1, March 1, or July 1 — check this box. The "born on the first" rule shifts all your enrollment dates one month earlier. This is a frequently missed detail that affects thousands of seniors each year and can change your exact coverage start date.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Click Calculate Effective Start Dates',
    text: 'The calculator instantly shows your exact Medicare Part A and Part B coverage effective start dates based on the official CMS (Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services) and SSA (Social Security Administration) rules. Review both dates carefully. Your Part B start date is the one that affects your doctor coverage and when you should schedule your first Medicare wellness visit.',
