  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       ELEMENT 8 — FAQ SECTION WITH SCHEMA
       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="medc-section" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
    <h2 id="faq-heading">Frequently Asked Questions About Medicare Effective Dates</h2>
    <FAQBlock items={faqs} />
  </section>

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       KEY TERMS AND ABBREVIATIONS
       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="medc-section" aria-labelledby="terms-heading">
    <h2 id="terms-heading">Key Terms Used on This Page</h2>
    <dl class="medc-terms">
      <div class="medc-term-row">
        <dt>IEP</dt>
        <dd>Initial Enrollment Period — your first and most important chance to sign up for Medicare. It is a 7-month window: the three months before your 65th birthday month, the birthday month itself, and three months after.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="medc-term-row">
        <dt>GEP</dt>
        <dd>General Enrollment Period — runs January 1 through March 31 each year. This is your fallback enrollment window if you missed your IEP and do not qualify for a Special Enrollment Period. Coverage starts the first of the month after you enroll.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="medc-term-row">
        <dt>SEP</dt>
        <dd>Special Enrollment Period — an 8-month window to sign up for Medicare Part B without penalty, triggered when you or your spouse stops working and loses active group health coverage from a current employer.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="medc-term-row">
        <dt>Part A</dt>
        <dd>Medicare hospital insurance — covers inpatient hospital stays, skilled nursing care, hospice, and some home health. Most people get Part A premium-free if they or their spouse paid Medicare taxes for at least 10 years (40 quarters).</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="medc-term-row">
        <dt>Part B</dt>
        <dd>Medicare medical insurance — covers doctor visits, outpatient services, preventive care, and medical equipment. The monthly premium in 2026 is $202.90 for most enrollees.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="medc-term-row">
        <dt>CMS</dt>
        <dd>Centers for Medicare &amp; Medicaid Services — the federal agency within the Department of Health and Human Services that administers Medicare, Medicaid, and CHIP (Children's Health Insurance Program).</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="medc-term-row">
        <dt>SSA</dt>
        <dd>Social Security Administration — the federal agency that processes Medicare enrollment applications. You sign up for Medicare through SSA even though CMS runs the program.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="medc-term-row">
        <dt>POMS</dt>
        <dd>Program Operations Manual System — the internal policy manual used by SSA employees to make Medicare decisions. It is publicly available and contains the technical rules behind every enrollment effective date calculation.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="medc-term-row">
        <dt>COBRA</dt>
        <dd>Consolidated Omnibus Budget Reconciliation Act — a federal law allowing you to continue employer group health coverage for up to 18–36 months after leaving a job. COBRA does NOT count as active employer coverage for Medicare enrollment purposes — the 8-month SEP starts when you leave work, not when COBRA ends.</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </section>

